---
/**
 * Project Dossier — Page Archetype
 *
 * A project page. Technical, structured, informative.
 * Always includes: serif title + summary, mono metadata block, architecture section, decisions/notes.
 * Never includes: marketing language, CTAs, feature comparison grids, testimonials.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Meta from '../../components/Meta.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title="Remarque (project)" description="A typography-first design system for editorial, technical, and personal web projects.">
  <article class="pt-[var(--space-9)]">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <nav class="remarque-breadcrumb mb-4" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol>
          <li><a href={base}>Home</a></li>
          <li><a href={`${base}projects`}>Projects</a></li>
          <li><span aria-current="page">Remarque</span></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="text-display font-display text-[var(--color-fg)]">Remarque</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[length:var(--text-body-lg)] leading-[var(--leading-body)] text-[var(--color-fg)] max-w-reading">
        A typography-first design system for editorial, technical, and personal web projects. Named for the remarque, the small sketch a printmaker adds in the margin of a plate, visible on the early proofs — the mark that says this was made by someone specific, with intention.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mb-12 p-6 border border-[var(--color-border)] rounded-[var(--radius-md)] bg-[var(--color-surface)]">
      <h2 class="text-label mb-4">Metadata</h2>
      <dl class="grid grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-x-8 gap-y-2 font-mono text-[length:var(--text-meta)] tracking-[var(--tracking-meta)]">
        <dt class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">Status</dt>
        <dd class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Active</dd>
        <dt class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">Stack</dt>
        <dd class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">CSS Custom Properties, Tailwind CSS, Astro</dd>
        <dt class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">Started</dt>
        <dd class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">2026-04-01</dd>
        <dt class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">License</dt>
        <dd class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">MIT</dd>
        <dt class="text-[var(--color-muted)]">Source</dt>
        <dd><a href="https://github.com/williamzujkowski/remarque" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-hover)] transition-colors duration-[var(--motion-fast)] ease-remarque">github.com/<wbr />williamzujkowski/<wbr />remarque</a></dd>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <Prose>
      <h2>Architecture</h2>

      <p>
        Remarque is built in layers, each with a specific responsibility:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Core Tokens</strong> (<code>tokens-core.css</code>) — The immutable identity: type scale, spacing, content widths, radius, and motion, as CSS custom properties. Overriding these is forking Remarque.</li>
        <li><strong>Palette Tokens</strong> (<code>tokens-palette.css</code>) — The sanctioned personalization surface: font slots, colors, accent, and the reading measure. Colors use OKLCH. <code>tokens.css</code> aggregates the two tiers.</li>
        <li><strong>Prose Styling</strong> (<code>prose.css</code>) — The <code>.remarque-prose</code> class handles long-form reading typography: headings, links, code blocks, blockquotes, tables, and images.</li>
        <li><strong>Tailwind Adapter</strong> (<code>theme.css</code> for Tailwind v4, <code>tailwind.config.js</code> for v3) — Maps tokens into utility classes without duplicating values.</li>
        <li><strong>Optional Modules</strong> — <code>essay.css</code>, <code>broadsheet.css</code>, <code>forms.css</code>, <code>chrome.css</code>, <code>print.css</code>, and the Palette Deck (<code>remarque-tokens/deck</code>), each imported only when a page needs it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Design Decisions</h2>

      <h3>Three-Font System</h3>
      <p>
        Newsreader for display, Inter for body, JetBrains Mono for metadata and code. Each font has a defined role and never crosses into another role’s territory. Three fonts is enough for clear hierarchy without confusion.
      </p>

      <h3>17px Minimum Body Text</h3>
      <p>
        Most systems default to 16px or smaller; USWDS, for one, asks for at least 16px. Remarque sets a floor one pixel higher, a deliberate choice for comfort in extended reading rather than a measured threshold.
      </p>

      <h3>38rem Reading Column</h3>
      <p>
        Chosen to sit inside the 45–75 characters per line that Robert Bringhurst gives as a satisfactory range for a single-column page (<em>The Elements of Typographic Style</em>, §2.1.2; Matthew Butterick allows 45–90). At 17px Inter, 38rem sets a median of about 71 characters per line — measured on rendered text, since <code>ch</code> arithmetic overstates the count (46rem, the earlier default, actually set 86).
      </p>

      <h3>OKLCH Color Space</h3>
      <p>
        Colors are defined in OKLCH, whose lightness axis is built to track perceived lightness. Two colors with the same OKLCH lightness look about equally light across hues, unlike HSL, where a yellow and a blue at the same L differ greatly in perceived brightness. That makes it practical to tune contrast by adjusting lightness alone.
      </p>

      <h2>Changelog</h2>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>2026-04-06</strong> — Initial release with specification, tokens, Tailwind config, and agent rules.</li>
        <li><strong>2026-04-08</strong> — Demo site built with Astro. All four page archetypes implemented.</li>
      </ul>
    </Prose>

    <nav class="content-reading mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-[var(--color-border)] flex" aria-label="More projects">
      <a href={`${base}projects`} class="footer-link -ml-2 font-mono text-[length:var(--text-meta)] tracking-[var(--tracking-meta)]">&larr; All projects</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
